From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrian Gielniewski <adrian.gielniewski@nordicsemi.no>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: mspi: dw: Skip SSIENR write when suspended

With PM device runtime enabled by default, pm_device_driver_init() leaves
the device suspended without calling the resume action. The controller
core is then inaccessible and the unconditional SSIENR write in dev_init()
causes a precise bus fault. A suspended controller is already disabled, so
skip the write in that case.

Signed-off-by: Adrian Gielniewski <adrian.gielniewski@nordicsemi.no>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mspi/mspi_dw.c b/drivers/mspi/mspi_dw.c
index 723b705801f..dfbebc1ddd4 100644
--- a/drivers/mspi/mspi_dw.c
+++ b/drivers/mspi/mspi_dw.c
@@ -2129,7 +2129,17 @@ static int dev_init(const struct device *dev)
 		return rc;
 	}
 
-	/* Make sure controller is disabled. */
+	/* Make sure controller is disabled. A device left suspended (PM runtime
+	 * enabled by default) has its core powered down and thus inaccessible,
+	 * but it is already disabled, so there is nothing to do in that case.
+	 */
+	enum pm_device_state state;
+
+	if (pm_device_state_get(dev, &state) == 0 &&
+	    state == PM_DEVICE_STATE_SUSPENDED) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	write_ssienr(dev, 0);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
2.43.0
